From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 15:22:52 +0200
Subject: Give spliced type binders their spliced type as info
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When a pickled quote with type holes is unpickled, the hole binders'
occurrences in the expansion are substituted by a TreeTypeMap, but a symbol
whose ClassInfo is unchanged by the map — for example an anonymous class whose
declarations, not parents, mention a binder — is not copied, and its members
keep referring to the binder symbol. The binder's pickled placeholder info is
`TypeAlias(Any)`, so such surviving references wrongly dealias to `Any` when a
later phase consults the member: under capture checking's recheck, a summoned
macro-built instance then fails refinement-member conformance
(`type Self = <binder>` vs the expected concrete type) with a confusing
"Object with Trait {...}^'sN does not conform" error, followed by "object
creation impossible".

Setting each binder's own info to its spliced type makes any surviving
reference dealias correctly, independently of which phase reads it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Proscala-Patch: splicealias
---
 .../tools/dotc/quoted/PickledQuotes.scala      | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/quoted/PickledQuotes.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/quoted/PickledQuotes.scala
index b47c20b3e5cdc2d7111ecfe7c0ca1d3b09fcb147..23726e003675e72461ae3d0f26f2abce47201ed6 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/quoted/PickledQuotes.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/quoted/PickledQuotes.scala
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@ package dotty.tools.dotc.quoted
 
 import dotty.tools.dotc.ast.Trees.*
 import dotty.tools.dotc.ast.{TreeTypeMap, tpd}
+import dotty.tools.dotc.config.Feature
 import dotty.tools.dotc.config.Printers.*
 import dotty.tools.dotc.core.Contexts.*
 import dotty.tools.dotc.core.Decorators.*
@@ -177,6 +178,23 @@ object PickledQuotes {
               case TypeHole.V2(types) =>
                 val Hole(_, idx, _, _) = tdef.rhs: @unchecked
                 PickledQuotes.quotedTypeToTree(types.nn.apply(idx))
+            // Under capture checking, point the binder's own info at the spliced type. The
+            // tree map below substitutes occurrences in the expansion's types, but a symbol
+            // whose ClassInfo is unchanged by the map (e.g. an anonymous class whose
+            // declarations — not parents — mention the binder) is not copied, and its members
+            // keep referring to this symbol. Its pickled placeholder info is `TypeAlias(Any)`,
+            // so such survivors wrongly dealias to `Any` when capture checking's recheck
+            // consults the member. The `@inferred` markers are stripped: as part of a member's
+            // alias they would fail the member's declared bounds in override checking.
+            // Confined to capture-checked runs: downstream macros that inspect types reaching
+            // through such surviving references observe the alias too, and existing code
+            // depends on the placeholder there.
+            if Feature.ccEnabledSomewhere then
+              def stripInferred(tp: Type): Type = tp match
+                case AnnotatedType(parent, annot) if annot.symbol == defn.InferredAnnot =>
+                  stripInferred(parent)
+                case _ => tp
+              tdef.symbol.info = TypeAlias(stripInferred(tree.tpe))
             (tdef.symbol, tree.tpe)
         }.toMap
         class ReplaceSplicedTyped extends TypeMap() {
